When filing for the registration of a new biological product, the requesting company must submit the following documents in addition to the registration petition forms and the payment receipt for the sanitary surveillance fee:

*   A declaration of the company's size (economic capacity) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   A copy of the company's Operating License and/or Sanitary Permit [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   A copy of the company's Authorization Certificate or its publication in the Official Gazette (DOU) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   A copy of the updated Technical Responsibility Certificate issued by the Regional Pharmacy Council [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Technical justification for the product registration [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   A copy of the Good Manufacturing Practices Certificate (CBPF) issued by Anvisa for all manufacturers of the active ingredient, bulk biological product, primary packaging, finished biological product, diluent, and adjuvant [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   A technical report containing information such as the names and addresses of manufacturers and storage locations, general product data (pharmaceutical form, composition, administration route, instructions for use, indications, contraindications, side effects, etc.) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31];
*   Complete reports of all non-clinical and clinical studies [RDC 55/2010, Art. 36].

